cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Donghyundoc (동현닥): a single-player pill-dropping puzzle laboratory in the manner of Dr. Mario, with the speed, virus level and pre-placed pills set through the esoteric language Donghyun-lang"
type: software
version: "0.01"
date-released: "2026-11-09"
authors:
  - family-names: Kim
    given-names: Dong Hyun
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9883-0229"
    affiliation: "Inha University College of Medicine"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Raspberry-Kim/donghyun-lab15"
url: "https://raspberry-kim.github.io/donghyun-lab15/"
abstract: >-
  Donghyundoc is a browser-based, noncommercial toy that follows only the
  skeleton of Dr. Mario (Nintendo R&D1, 1990): two-cell pills are dropped
  into an 8x16 bottle onto viruses, four cells of one colour in a row or
  column vanish, unsupported pills fall and chain, and clearing every virus
  ends the level. The doctor is Podongi, the maker's Maltese dog, using the
  first PNG image that serves as the icon of the Donghyun series; the three
  viruses are newly drawn 9x9 pixel faces, and pills come in capsule, tablet
  and syringe shapes. The speed (slow, medium, fast), the virus level (1-20)
  and the number of pre-placed pills are chosen through a program written in
  the esoteric programming language Donghyun-lang. Input is keyboard and
  gamepad only, with fullscreen; the game is saved in three browser slots and
  can be exported to and imported from a .dhsave file. All other graphics,
  colours and sounds are generated by code; no asset of the original game is
  used or extracted. Dr. Mario and Mario are trademarks of Nintendo; this
  work is unaffiliated. The MIT license applies to the Donghyundoc code and
  documentation; the page fonts are under the SIL Open Font License. See
  LICENSE and CREDITS.md.
keywords:
  - puzzle game
  - Dr. Mario
  - esoteric programming language
  - JavaScript
